  "investigation": [
    "The latest RV32 generic PCS, circle polynomial and scalar backend files are already byte-identical to this worktree; no wholesale code import is needed.",
    "The existing tiled committer retains every minimal n coefficient and drops wide LDE columns at the compact threshold, so it is compatible with full CPU coset/previous-mask evaluation.",
    "The 2n commitment LDE and 4n composition quotient canonical odd cosets are disjoint; both evaluations are required, while their coefficient owner is reused.",
    "OODS uses coefficient plans; coefficient-backed FRI quotient contributions are folded by sample/domain groups before evaluation.",
    "Selective opening re-expands only queried FFT branches because full 2n LDE columns were intentionally discarded. Retaining all LDE columns to avoid this tail would trade substantial memory for a small observed stage.",
    "Default combined CPU preparation requires 65 columns. An eight-column streaming batch cannot select it. At log21, the default 256MiB source-plus-LDE staging budget caps batches near ten columns, so raising the nominal batch count to 128 alone still does not select that hook."
  ],
  "owned_arena_recommendation": {
    "status": "future experiment only; not adopted",
    "precondition": "Separate row-major interaction metadata removes the dependency on original CPU main values after main commitment.",
    "existing_api": "CommitmentSchemeProver.commitOwnedWithRecorderAndBacking",
    "ownership": "Allocate CPU matrix plus a small reserved provider-multiplicity tail in one arena. Copy only provider multiplicities into that tail: their original count vectors remain live until challenge-dependent provider generation. Transfer descriptor and backing ownership exactly once on success and failure.",
    "current_api_gap": "Only a single backing arena reaches the compact streaming zero-copy route; multiple owners detach/copy every source. The owned convenience dispatcher also switches at 128 columns and the monolithic arena lane depends on the 65-column fused threshold. Avoid encoding these backend thresholds in the frontend. A future explicit owned-streaming-with-backing PCS boundary should make eligibility and ownership uniform.",
    "gates": [
      "Same complete proof bytes and fresh receiver acceptance.",
      "Allocation-failure and double-free/leak coverage for arena transfer.",
      "Both small and large column sets, all mixed domain heights and previous masks.",
      "Matched whole-job wall time and charged peak, including metadata and provider copies."
    ]
  },
  "rv32_lessons": {
    "source_commit": "66e26f6ed",
    "references": [
      "design/riscv-proving-stack/performance/closed-tiling-m5-20261028.md",
      "design/riscv-proving-stack/performance/native-domain-tiling-m5-20261028.md"
    ],
    "lesson": "Complete proof closure and independently sized domains matter. More execution proofs and blindly larger native domains regressed complete cost in those workload-specific experiments; their measured timings do not transfer to RV64 ECDSA."
  },
